  <data key="d7">Interactions in the Indian Ocean and East Asia were significantly impacted by the spread of Islam and the political changes brought by the Caliphates.</data>
  <data key="d8">cultural exchange,trade</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86</data>
  <data key="d10">/kaggle/working/reproduce_MegaRAG/World_History_Volume_1_run/dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
  <data key="d11">1787393103</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pax Mongolica" target="The Steppe Empire of the Mongols">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Pax Mongolica is a key concept that describes the stability and peace achieved under the Mongol Empire, which is synonymous with the rise of the Steppe Empire.</data>
  <data key="d8">cultural exchange,historical impact</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-4a7bd606960e970df3415af494e95c38</data>
  <data key="d10">/kaggle/working/reproduce_MegaRAG/World_History_Volume_1_run/dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
  <data key="d11">1787393103</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pax Mongolica" target="Song China">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The peace established by Pax Mongolica allowed for interaction and trade between Song China and other regions, exemplifying cultural exchange.</data>
  <data key="d8">cultural interaction,trade</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-4a7bd606960e970df3415af494e95c38</data>
  <data key="d10">/kaggle/working/reproduce_MegaRAG/World_History_Volume_1_run/dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
  <data key="d11">1787393103</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pax Mongolica" target="Ottomans, Mamluks, and Ming">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">These empires emerged in a context influenced by the Pax Mongolica, which affected their development and interactions.</data>
  <data key="d8">development,historical context</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-4a7bd606960e970df3415af494e95c38</data>
  <data key="d10">/kaggle/working/reproduce_MegaRAG/World_History_Volume_1_run/dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
  <data key="d11">1787393103</data>
</edge>
<edge source="The Steppe Empire of the Mongols" target="Chinggis Khan">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Chinggis Khan founded and expanded the Mongol Empire, playing a crucial role in establishing the foundations of the Steppe Empire.</data>
  <data key="d8">expansion,founder</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-4a7bd606960e970df3415af494e95c38</data>
  <data key="d10">/kaggle/working/reproduce_MegaRAG/World_History_Volume_1_run/dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
  <data key="d11">1787393103</data>
</edge>
<edge source="The Black Death" target="Climate Change in the Fourteenth Century">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Black Death was worsened by climate change factors that caused famines, contributing to its spread and severity.</data>
  <data key="d8">environmental impact,epidemic</data>
